{
    "_doc": "Demand of permission_sex_unprotected (its demandEventID, Docs/Interactions/Step06FPermissionsImplementationPlan.md P5b part 3): started by ActionPackage.TryStopForDemand when the granter ACCEPTED a penis-in-vagina act but has not allowed unprotected sex - the act is stopped before it begins (no effects, no refusal costs). self = the requester (permission holder), evTarget = the granter. A refusal never comes here (plain OnAPRefuse). Code (ActionPackage.SendDemandEvent) builds the condom answers into StoredOptions[demandOptions] - the wearer is whoever's penis the act uses: put it on yourself / on $evTarget$ now (arms + an accessible condom; the act resumes with its accepted result kept), or let $evTarget$ put it on you by hand / mouth (the condom command runs with its acceptance kept; the act does not resume by itself). Unavailable answers stay visible, disabled, with the command's own reason. The event's own options: ignore the demand (apCallback: records the scene push - no demand for this pair again in this scene - and resumes the act) or give up (failCallback). An NPC requester decides in code (put it on now if possible, else ignore) and the event starts at that answer's line (br_condom_self / br_condom_target / br_npc_push / br_end). The granter's demand is the kojo permission_sex_unprotected_Demand. File name contains sex: safe mode skips it.",
    "Events": {
        "list": [
            {
                "ID": "OnAPRefuse_Unprotected",
                "SelfValidator": { "chara_conditions": [ { "parameters": [ "exists" ] } ] },
                "events": [
                    {
                        "$type": "Event+EventEntry+EventEntry_Branch, Assembly-CSharp",
